The lists below were taken from the package.json "license" field of the
packages installed while developing LocalCast 0.1.0. Run `npm ls` against
package-lock.json for the full tree on your machine.

Direct dependencies
- fastify — MIT
- @fastify/multipart — MIT
- @fastify/websocket — MIT
- qrcode — MIT
- sharp — Apache-2.0
- react, react-dom — MIT
- vite — MIT
- typescript — Apache-2.0
- tsx — MIT
- ws — MIT

Fonts bundled into the web build
- @fontsource/fraunces — OFL-1.1
- @fontsource/outfit — OFL-1.1

Notable transitive packages
- @img/sharp-libvips-* (the prebuilt libvips shipped for sharp) — the installed
  package metadata says LGPL-3.0-or-later. LocalCast does not modify libvips.
  It is loaded as a shared native library through sharp. LGPL obligations stay
  with that library; upstream source is published by the libvips and sharp projects
  (https://github.com/libvips/libvips and https://github.com/lovell/sharp).
- lightningcss — MPL-2.0 (used by Vite at build time)
- fast-uri, light-my-request, secure-json-parse — BSD-3-Clause
- tslib — 0BSD

If a future sharp release changes the libvips license field, trust the
installed package metadata over this file.
